      <description>Last December, India’s airports were a chaotic mess as IndiGo, the nation’s largest carrier, canceled thousands of flights because of a pilot shortage. This year, it's the turn of another airline to leave passengers stranded — SpiceJet Ltd.’s cash crunch is so severe that it is unable to operate more than half of its scheduled journeys, according to The Economic Times.</description>
