    <item>
      <title>Nvidia Embodies George Soros’ Reflexivity Theory in AI Era</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-24/nvidia-embodies-george-soros-reflexivity-theory-in-ai-era</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">8e7f767dc1738b770329343b</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:30:10 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The George Soros theory of reflexivity — which says that stock prices influence fundamentals as much as they reflect them — has been everywhere in financial markets and the economy. Surging enthusiasm for artificial intelligence has let companies raise vast amounts of capital in debt and equity markets, money they have spent on semiconductors and the like, generating hundreds of billions of profits for Nvidia Corp. and other chipmakers, and sending stocks ever higher.</description>
      <dc:creator>Jonathan Levin</dc:creator>
